{"name":"Pompeius Blue","hex":"#77a8ab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pompey","blocks":[{"text":"Gnaeus Pompeius Magnus, known in English as Pompey or Pompey the Great, was a Roman general and statesman who was prominent in the final decades of the Roman Republic. As a young man, he was a partisan and protégé of the dictator Sulla, after whose death he achieved significant military and political success."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/%28Venice%29_Pompey_the_Great%2C_Museo_Archeologico_Nazionale.jpg/330px-%28Venice%29_Pompey_the_Great%2C_Museo_Archeologico_Nazionale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pompey"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Roman_Province_of_Africa_in_146_BC.png/500px-Roman_Province_of_Africa_in_146_BC.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Roman_Province_of_Africa_in_146_BC.png/500px-Roman_Province_of_Africa_in_146_BC.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roman Province of Africa","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoman_Province_of_Africa_in_146_BC.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Pompey%2C_aureus%2C_71_BC%2C_RRC_402-1.png/500px-Pompey%2C_aureus%2C_71_BC%2C_RRC_402-1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Pompey%2C_aureus%2C_71_BC%2C_RRC_402-1.png/500px-Pompey%2C_aureus%2C_71_BC%2C_RRC_402-1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aureus minted by Pompey for his second triumph in 71 BC, featuring the head of Africa on the obverse (celebrating his victory against Hiarbas). The reverse shows Pompey in his triumphal chariot, with his son Gnaeus seated before and Victory flying above.[52]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APompey%2C_aureus%2C_71_BC%2C_RRC_402-1.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Mithridates_VI_Louvre.jpg/500px-Mithridates_VI_Louvre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Mithridates_VI_Louvre.jpg/1280px-Mithridates_VI_Louvre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Mithridates_VI_Louvre.jpg/500px-Mithridates_VI_Louvre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bust of Mithridates of Pontus in the Louvre, Paris","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMithridates_VI_Louvre.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Lodovico_Pogliaghi_-_Pompey_in_the_Holy_of_Holies_in_Jerusalem%2C_63_BC.png/500px-Lodovico_Pogliaghi_-_Pompey_in_the_Holy_of_Holies_in_Jerusalem%2C_63_BC.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Lodovico_Pogliaghi_-_Pompey_in_the_Holy_of_Holies_in_Jerusalem%2C_63_BC.png/500px-Lodovico_Pogliaghi_-_Pompey_in_the_Holy_of_Holies_in_Jerusalem%2C_63_BC.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pompey in the Holy of Holies of the Jerusalem Temple, drawing by Lodovico Pogliaghi (1883)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALodovico_Pogliaghi_-_Pompey_in_the_Holy_of_Holies_in_Jerusalem%2C_63_BC.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Faustus_Cornelius_Sulla%2C_AR_denarius%2C_56_BC%2C_RRC_426-4a.jpg/500px-Faustus_Cornelius_Sulla%2C_AR_denarius%2C_56_BC%2C_RRC_426-4a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Faustus_Cornelius_Sulla%2C_AR_denarius%2C_56_BC%2C_RRC_426-4a.jpg/500px-Faustus_Cornelius_Sulla%2C_AR_denarius%2C_56_BC%2C_RRC_426-4a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Denarius minted in 56 BC by Pompey's supporter Faustus Sulla[e][88][89]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFaustus_Cornelius_Sulla%2C_AR_denarius%2C_56_BC%2C_RRC_426-4a.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/First_Triumvirate_of_Caesar%2C_Crassius_and_Pompey.jpg/500px-First_Triumvirate_of_Caesar%2C_Crassius_and_Pompey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o